    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\nnvim_buf_call() can crash inside an expression evaluated for a window\r\noutside the current tabpage. This can happen when:\r\n\r\n- A scheduled buffer update calls changed_common(), which updates folds\r\n  in every window displaying the buffer, including windows in other\r\n  tabpages. If the update clears the buffer, vim.treesitter.foldexpr()\r\n  calls nvim_buf_call(0, ...).\r\n- nvim_eval_statusline() evaluates a statusline expression for a window\r\n  in another tabpage, and the expression calls nvim_buf_call(0, ...).\r\n\r\nExpression evaluation temporarily sets curwin and curbuf to the window\r\nand buffer being evaluated, while leaving curtab unchanged.\r\nnvim_buf_call(0, ...) requests that buffer, so ctx_switch() reuses curwin.\r\nHowever, its win_valid() assertion searches only windows in curtab.\r\nThe assertion therefore fails because curwin belongs to another tabpage,\r\neven though the window still exists.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nUse win_valid_any_tab() to check that the buffer-context window exists.\r\nThis allows ctx_switch() to reuse curwin when the requested buffer is\r\nalready curbuf, even if curwin belongs to another tabpage.\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n* A unit test for `ctx_switch`\r\n* Functional tests exercising the cases discussed above",
