            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I think we can *drop* the functional tests, and keep only the unit test.\r\n\r\nThe initial motivation was the assertion failure I encountered while using octo.nvim. With AI, I reduced it to the foldexpr test in this PR. This PR directly fixes that assertion failure.\r\n\r\nBut then it occured to me that foldexpr evaluation can be considered buggy on its own: it sets the current window and buffer to those of another tabpage, but leaves the current tabpage unchanged. I have a separate AI-authored fix (https://github.com/tomtomjhj/neovim/commit/c41833492bb69705737757c730b73512be4d4034) for that. Looking for another assertion trigger revealed a similar issue in statusline, with a corresponding fix (https://github.com/tomtomjhj/neovim/commit/21c633dc3dca102d9aaada5a71d0953546f5d72b, also AI-authored). I'll review and make a PR for them separately.\r\n\r\nWith those fixes applied, the functional tests here pass even without this PR. Their coverage would therefore belong with the folding and statusline fixes, so I would prefer to remove them here.\r\n\r\nThis PR still makes sense independently. Reusing the current window does not need to require the window to belong to the current tabpage.\r\n",
